    {
      "id": "FZD-03",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-fixed-zero-block",
      "title": "Height separation and the exponent in the fixed-modulus density bound",
      "statement": "The count of separated pairs is O((mT)^{24(1−σ)}(log(mT))^{10}). A block contributes at most 4U^{2−2σ}(1+log(2U))³G/θ². The nonprincipal block sum has logarithmic exponent seven and the principal sum has exponent nine before the common enlargement.",
